OL,3,GNEWSAThe hero dinner lady who died
OL,4,Ashielding five children in the Aberfan
OL,5,Adisaster
OL,6,
OL,7,FAn Aberfan disaster survivor who was
OL,8,Fsaved by a dinner lady has spoken
OL,9,Fpublicly for the first time about his
OL,10,Fhero.
OL,12,FPaul Harries, who was six, was one of
OL,13,Ffive children found alive under the
OL,14,Fbody of Nansi Williams.
OL,16,FIt was on 21 October 1966 that a coal
OL,17,Ftip above the village of Aberfan
OL,18,Fcollapsed, engulfing Pantglas Junior
OL,19,FSchool and nearby homes.
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
